/P 118 0 R
/E (Motions are formal requests made by delegates to influence the meeting's procedures. They guide the flow of the debate and include requests such as opening or closing the debate, introducing a moderated or unmoderated caucus, or adjourning the meeting. Each motion is put to a vote, and if approved, it dictates how the committee will proceed, whether by allowing structured speeches, facilitating informal discussions, or ending the session. Motions help manage the agenda and ensure an organized and efficient conference.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [7 8]
>>
