/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 119 0 R
/E (An Unmoderated Caucus is a break from formal debate where delegates move freely around the room to discuss, negotiate, and draft resolutions or working papers. Unlike a Moderated Caucus, there is no formal speaking order or time limits. Delegates use this time to collaborate informally, build alliances, and refine their positions before presenting them in the formal sessions. To propose an Unmoderated Caucus, a delegate must raise a motion by saying, "The delegate of [Country] would like to raise a motion to start an unmoderated caucus for [Duration].")
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [4]
>>
